138664, "top": [["-", -0.0003641314688138664], ["The", -10.502511024475098]]}], "text": "Here's a summary of the session notes in 8 bullet points:\n\n- **Scope & context:** A two-part session (Context A: Claude Opus 5.5, 09-26 to 09-28; Context B: Claude Sonnet 5.5, resumed 10-01) rebuilt the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D, Intel Arc A770 16GB), switching the GPU driver from i915 to **xe** between the two contexts.\n\n- **Main work:** The session covered a PKGBUILD rework, a 3000+ commit rebuild series (b10146 \u2192 b12321), an LLAMA_SUBPROCESS ABI trap, SYCL graphs, a oneDNN A/B comparison, a oneAPI 2026.0 \u2192 2026.1 swap (DLE), a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash patch, 256-GRF kernels, and a \"12-vs-18 t/s\" decode investigation.\n\n- **Key technical finding:** A critical ABI incompatibility trap was identified in the `d37dd50bb` commit, and a separate IGC crash in `4e7400c3a` (DG2 XMX-gather) was patched; the session also investigated decode throughput discrepancies.\n\n- **Documentation approach:** The notes were written thoroughly at the user's request, with claims tagged by evidence type (**[verified live]**, **[log]**, **[transcript]**), and evidence files copied to a dedicated directory with SHA-256 checksums.\n\n-"}